{
  "$schema": "./engines.schema.json",
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Single source of truth for serpapi_fdw. Consumed by (1) the Rust wrapper via include_str! (import foreign schema DDL, param mapping, row mapping), and (2) scripts/gen.py which emits sql/20_generated.sql (composite types + public functions).",
    "params: `name` is the SQL column/argument name; `api` is the SerpApi query parameter (defaults to name). `default` may reference a server option as `server:<option>`.",
    "Optional-parameter convention: text '' / int|numeric -1 / bool false mean 'unset' and are omitted from the request. The wrapper echoes exactly what it was given so Postgres' local recheck passes.",
    "pagination.kind: none | start (step N) | page (1-based) | next_page_token (from serpapi_pagination.next_page_token).",
    "columns: `path` is a dotted path into one result object of `block`; types map to Postgres types text|int|bigint|numeric|bool|jsonb.",
    "Every typed table also gets: pages int (param), search_id text (param+result), page int (result), raw jsonb (result). Those are added by the generators, not listed here."
  ],
  "common_params": [
    {
      "name": "gl",
      "type": "text",
      "default": "server:default_gl",
      "doc": "Country code, e.g. in"
    },
    {
      "name": "hl",
      "type": "text",
      "default": "server:default_hl",
      "doc": "Language code, e.g. en, hi, ta"
    }
  ],
